{
  "_about": "Golden cases for backend/services/rate_scenario.scenario_in_the_money and the SCENARIO_ITM_SQL fragment (Rate Lever, audit wow-stage-1). Each step is a different market rate: fn_in_the_money(fn_rate_spread(note, market + step / 10000), equity, min_spread, min_equity). Cases come from a search of eighth-point coupons (0.05875 .. 0.06875) against FRED-like prints (0.0612, 0.0630, 0.0655) across the grid, with Python float arithmetic. raw_spread_bps is (note - (market + step / 10000)) * 10000 as a Python float; bin_shift_spread_bps is the WRONG method (rate_spread_bps(note, market) - step), kept so the tests can prove it disagrees. A null note is the gated no-signal case (0 bps at every step). tests/unit/test_rate_scenario.py recomputes every case; the nightly tests/integration/test_rate_sensitivity_parity.py runs them through the UC functions.",
